IngeCAD's vendored LibreDWG patches, on top of the 0.14.8597 release.

Every hunk below is either an open pull request against LibreDWG/libredwg,
taken from the pull request's own head (not from a local branch, which is
how a stale draft of #1375 once shipped here and corrupted MTEXT in pre-r2007
drawings), or a fix of ours not yet sent upstream. Each one disappears from
this file the moment it is merged and we take a newer release. #1392 left
with 0.14.8597.

Open pull requests:
  #1358 decode: r2004 sections whose declared size exceeds the page estimate
  #1359 dwg: skip unresolvable owned entities instead of ending the layout
  #1360 decode: resync the object map when a modular char fails to parse
  #1364 decode_r11: a missing table sentinel must not reject the drawing
  #1365 dwg2SVG: the output was blank for four independent reasons
  #1368 r11: give pre-R13 drawings their paper space BLOCK_HEADER
  #1369 TIMEBLL: one julian-day fraction, three wrong conventions for it
  #1371 in_dxf: store subentities as AutoCAD does
  #1372 out_dxf: do not write stale subentities a second time
  #1373 out_dxf: a block header without BLOCK must not abort the whole DXF
  #1375 in_dxf: convert r2007+ UTF-8 strings to the pre-r2007 target codepage
  #1378 r13/r14: the entity linetype never survived a DXF import
  #1381 encode: writing r11/r12 from an r13+ source produced an unreadable DWG
  #1382 dwg_next_handle: scan all objects for the max
  #1385 in_dxf: MINSERT column/row count default to 1
  #1387 out_dxf: preserve an unparseable entity as a proxy
  #1422 in_dxf: keep each application's EED apart when an object has several
  #1423 in_dxf: resolve the ACAD EED application through the APPID table
  #1424 out_dxf: emit the annotation-scale context data

Not yet sent (see tools/libredwg-patches/README.md, 2026-09-27):
  in_dxf: DIMENSION_ANG3PT group 16; accents in pre-r2007 dictionary keys;
          FIELDLIST fields
  proxies: class number, graphics in AcDbProxyEntity, no phantom proxy_data,
           format version packing and clamping
  encode: a large entity preview no longer skips its bytes

